# Haemophilia Data Ingestion & Scheduling System

A production-ready data acquisition, normalization, and scheduling pipeline that periodically ingests haemophilia and hemophilia-related information from multiple authoritative public sources into a centralized relational database.

> [!NOTE]
> **Pure Data Pipeline**: This system contains **NO AI integrations, LLM calls, or embeddings**. It focuses solely on data acquisition, transformation, schema normalization, rate limiting, and persistent scheduling.

---

## Supported Data Sources

| Source | Identifier / Key Fields | Data Type | Authentication |
|---|---|---|---|
| **ClinicalTrials.gov** | NCTId, BriefTitle, Status, Conditions, Interventions | Clinical Trial Registrations | None required |
| **PubMed (NCBI)** | PMID, ArticleTitle, Abstract, Authors, Journal, DOI | Peer-Reviewed Medical Literature | Optional API key (`NCBI_API_KEY`) |
| **OpenFDA** | SafetyReportID, Drug Names, Reactions, Recall Numbers | FDA Adverse Events & Recalls | Optional API key (`OPENFDA_API_KEY`) |
| **WHO ICTRP** | TrialID, Public/Scientific Title, Sponsor, Countries | Global Clinical Trial Registries | None (bulk export) |
| **medRxiv** | DOI, Title, Abstract, Authors, Version, Category | Medical Preprints | None required |
| **arXiv** | ArxivID, Title, Summary/Abstract, Authors, Categories | Life Sciences & PK Modeling Preprints | None required |
| **USPTO Patents** | Application Number, Title, Abstract, Applicant | Patent Filings & Grants | API key required (`USPTO_API_KEY`) |
| **SEC EDGAR** | CIK, Accession Number (ADSH), Form 10-K/10-Q, Excerpts | Corporate & Biotech Filings | User-Agent header (required by SEC) |

