## Database Schema Design

The database uses a normalized relational schema with 3 core tables:

### 1. `raw_items` (Unified Normalized Data Store)
- `id` (VARCHAR 36, UUID Primary Key)
- `source_name` (VARCHAR 100, Indexed) — e.g. `"ClinicalTrials.gov"`, `"PubMed (NCBI)"`
- `source_id` (VARCHAR 500) — Original ID from source API (e.g. `NCT04567890`, `38123456`)
- `source_url` (TEXT, Indexed) — Direct permalink to source record
- `title` (TEXT) — Item title or headline
- `raw_content` (TEXT) — Full parsed text (abstract, summary, protocol, or filing excerpt)
- `date_published` (DATETIME with timezone) — Original publication or filing date
- `date_ingested` (DATETIME with timezone, Indexed) — Ingestion timestamp
- `metadata` (TEXT / JSON) — JSON string with source-specific structured attributes
- `is_active` (BOOLEAN) — Active flag for soft deletion or tracking outdated records
- **Constraint**: `UNIQUE(source_name, source_id)` ensures **idempotent upserts**.

### 2. `ingestor_logs` (Audit Log)
- `id` (INTEGER, Autoincrement Primary Key)
- `ingestor_name` (VARCHAR 100, Indexed) — Identifier of the ingestor
- `run_timestamp` (DATETIME with timezone) — Run start timestamp
- `items_fetched` (INTEGER) — Total items returned by API
- `items_stored` (INTEGER) — Newly inserted items
- `items_skipped` (INTEGER) — Skipped or existing items updated
- `success` (BOOLEAN) — True if run succeeded without unhandled errors
- `error_message` (TEXT) — Exception traceback if failed
- `last_cursor` (TEXT) — Pagination token/offset saved at run completion
- `duration_seconds` (FLOAT) — Execution time in seconds

### 3. `scheduling_metadata` (State Persistence)
- `ingestor_name` (VARCHAR 100, Primary Key) — Ingestor identifier
- `last_run_timestamp` (DATETIME with timezone) — Last execution timestamp
- `next_scheduled_run` (DATETIME with timezone) — Next planned run
- `run_interval_minutes` (INTEGER) — Configured run interval in minutes
- `is_enabled` (BOOLEAN) — Enable/disable flag
- `last_cursor` (TEXT) — Resumption token for paginated APIs
- `consecutive_failures` (INTEGER) — Failure counter for alerting

---

## Setup Instructions

### 1. Prerequisites
- Python 3.9+ installed (`python3 --version`)

### 2. Activate Virtual Environment
The virtual environment is already created at `.venv`:
```bash
cd data-ingestion-system
source .venv/bin/activate
```

### 3. Install Dependencies
```bash
pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
pip install -e .
```

### 4. Configure Environment Variables
Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and set your preferred settings:
```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

Key environment variables in `.env`:
- `DATABASE_URL`: `sqlite+aiosqlite:///./haemophilia_data.db` (default) or PostgreSQL `postgresql+asyncpg://user:pass@localhost:5432/haemophilia_db`
- `LOG_LEVEL`: `INFO` (or `DEBUG`, `WARNING`, `ERROR`)
- `INGESTORS_ENABLED`: Comma-separated list of enabled ingestors
- `NCBI_API_KEY`: (Optional) Free API key for PubMed
- `OPENFDA_API_KEY`: (Optional) Free API key for OpenFDA
- `USPTO_API_KEY`: (Optional) Free API key for USPTO Patents
- `SEC_EDGAR_USER_AGENT`: `AppName admin@example.com` (required for SEC EDGAR)

---

## Usage & CLI Commands

### List Registered Ingestors & Schedules
```bash
python run.py --list-ingestors
```
Output:
```
============================================================
Registered Haemophilia Ingestors
============================================================
  • clinical_trials    [ENABLED ] Interval:   1440 min (ClinicalTrials.gov)
  • pubmed             [ENABLED ] Interval:   1440 min (PubMed (NCBI))
  • openfda            [ENABLED ] Interval:   1440 min (OpenFDA)
  • who_ictrp          [ENABLED ] Interval:  10080 min (WHO ICTRP)
  • medrxiv            [ENABLED ] Interval:   1440 min (medRxiv)
  • arxiv              [ENABLED ] Interval:   1440 min (arXiv)
  • patents            [ENABLED ] Interval:  10080 min (USPTO Patents)
  • sec_edgar          [ENABLED ] Interval:  10080 min (SEC EDGAR)
============================================================
```

### Initialize Database Schema
```bash
python run.py --init-db
```

### Run a Single Ingestor Once
```bash
python run.py --run-once clinical_trials
python run.py --run-once pubmed
python run.py --run-once openfda
python run.py --run-once arxiv
```

### Run All Enabled Ingestors Once
```bash
python run.py --run-all-once
```

### Start Background Scheduler Mode
Runs continuously in the foreground, executing jobs at their configured intervals:
```bash
python run.py
```

---

## Database Migrations (Alembic)

Run migrations to create or update schema:
```bash
alembic upgrade head
```

Create a new migration after model changes:
```bash
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add new column"
```

---

## Running Tests

All unit tests use **mocked HTTP responses** with `respx` and in-memory SQLite fixtures (no live API calls):

```bash
pytest -v
```

Run tests with test coverage:
```bash
pytest --cov=app --cov-report=term-missing
```

---

## Querying Ingested Data

Using Python async session:
```python
import asyncio
from sqlalchemy import select
from app.database import get_session, RawItemModel

async def sample_query():
    async with get_session() as session:
        stmt = select(RawItemModel).where(RawItemModel.source_name == "ClinicalTrials.gov").limit(5)
        result = await session.execute(stmt)
        items = result.scalars().all()
        for item in items:
            print(f"[{item.source_id}] {item.title}")
            print(f"URL: {item.source_url}")
            print(f"Metadata: {item.metadata_dict}\n")

asyncio.run(sample_query())
```

Using SQLite CLI:
```bash
sqlite3 haemophilia_data.db "SELECT source_name, count(*) FROM raw_items GROUP BY source_name;"
sqlite3 haemophilia_data.db "SELECT * FROM ingestor_logs ORDER BY run_timestamp DESC LIMIT 10;"
```
